cases.json and invalid.json contain the test cases of that file in the
format of tests/Corpus. tools/extract_icalnet.py makes them. Changes: each
block becomes one case; the comment becomes "description"; a DATE value of
DTSTART gets ";VALUE=DATE"; "EXCEPTION:" becomes "expectedError"; the RRULE
that Ical.Net rejects at parse time goes to invalid.json; the cases that
test the Ical.Net year-9999 limit are not copied.

